{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453013-help-mage-20th-archetype-characters","id":1453013,"title":"Help - Mage 20th Archetype Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-20T22:02:56-07:00","id":1453013,"title":"Help - Mage 20th Archetype Characters","content":"Long story short: I'm theorycrafting some Mages (since getting a Chronicle together was near impossible BEFORE this Year and a Half of Nightmares), but I have trouble keeping the Char Gen rules straight (this book is horribly laid out, could do with more page refs and not having half the important stuff bundled together in the Appendix and in three other volumes) and am unsure of how to build them. So I thought: someone should draw up some examples to build from. Think of it as a thought exercise/building a new player resource and chime in with any other 'basic' mage ideas (and don't think I'm lazy and pawning the heavy lifting off on y'all...Please?).<br /> <br /> First up: a Witch. As in, a 90s Hollywood witch. A 'The Craft' witch. Apart from the Tradition (either Verbena or Hollow) and/or the Spheres (Life/Prime, maybe?). I'm lost<br /> <br /> Second: an Investigator. Uses magick to augment their natural abilities. This one I am completely clueless on, but I play detectives in everything, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23581-professordetective","name":"ProfessorDetective","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T04:03:48-07:00","id":1453018,"title":"","content":"The Witches in &quot;The Craft&quot; are best simulated as either Orphans or Hollow Ones. Although the woman in the store who sold them their books and supplies was Verena. <br /> <br /> They seemed to use the Spheres of Mind, Spirit, Forces, and Life. Certainly the 'Love' spell used mind. The healing spells used Life. The levitations and similar used forces. And there were many spirit invocations.<br /> <br /> Your investigator sounds to me like a Hermetic or an Etherite. First level sphere magic enhances the awareness of that sphere. Forces at that level would allow you to see the warmth left over from recent footsteps. Matter would let you know what grains of power are as efficiently as spectroscopic analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T05:03:54-07:00","id":1453024,"title":"","content":"The investigator could be a whole bunch of characters IMO and could be extremely interesting.<br /> The Hermetic or Etherite as Astromancer mentioned are good, but maybe he's an Ecstatic who shows up to the crime scene's high all the time, though he hides it extremely well (or he thinks he does). Maybe he's an Iteration X cyborg with faulty implants (maybe an ADEI for the super-enhanced mental capacity and the Skeletal Enhancement for the added suvivability, both of which are not noticeable) who is always in pain from them, so he's always cranky as hell, but he has a heart of gold (not literally, it's probably Primium). You could make any Tradition/Convention work for this character.<br /> <br /> In any case, basic investigation and forensics on a human(ish) level would mostly be Matter 1, but most spheres at level 1 or 2 would make him supernaturally gifted. With Correspondence/Data he could figure out exact bullet trajectories. With Entropy he could just let Fate and Fortune guide him to the most relevant evidence. With Mind he could read witnesses' emotions or even thoughts, or enhance his own mental attributes to be a veritable Sherlock Holmes. With Prime and/or Spirit his investigative power could extend more into the supernatural, sensing if the crime was perpetrated by ghosts or mages or something else. With Prime/Matter he could read psychic impressions left on the murder weapon. With Time 1 maybe he just has a bizarrely accurate sense of timing which is more of an interesting quirk, but with Time 2 (and maybe Entropy 1), he can actually just see what happened for himself. In any and all cases, he is a walking one person crime solver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 06-21-2021, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T08:53:37-07:00","id":1453043,"title":"","content":"I think most of the premade character templates from the original and revised Tradition books are easily adaptable to M20. <br /> <br /> About 10 years ago, as a creative exercise, I did outlines for alternate Mage books in the 90s, including character templates.<br /> <br /> Initial four premade characters from an alternate Storytellers Screen booklet:<ul><li><b>Club DJ</b> (Dynamic; Virtual Adept or Cult of Ecstasy) - a mainstay of the underground club and rave scene, specializing in Forces and Mind magic focused through electronic dance music and DJ systems. (Correspondence 1, Forces 2, Mind 2, Time 1)</li> <li><b>Spiritual Guru</b> (Pattern; Dreamspeaker or Akashic Brotherhood) - a teacher and guide offering insight into spiritual harmony and mental peace, using Mind and Spirit magic focused through meditation, ritual, and speech. (Life 2, Mind 2, Spirit 2)</li> <li><b>Avenging Witch</b> (Primordial; Verbena or Euthanatos) - an angry young person full of resentment and judgment, using Entropy and Life magic focused through classic and neopagan witchcraft rituals and curses. (Entropy 3, Life 3 or Entropy 2, Forces 2, Life 2)</li> <li><b>Knight Magus</b> (Questing; Order of Hermes or Celestial Chorus) - a modern knight-errant in search of wisdom and enlightenment, using Correspondence, Forces and Prime magic focused through their signature weapon and high ritual rites. (Correspondence 2, Forces 2, Prime 2)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And from the theoretical alternate Players Guide, all of these are based on the idea of being tied into the mundane world as something akin to urban fantasy characters:<ul><li><b>Urban Samurai</b> (Akashic Brotherhood; Primordial) - a street kid who found discipline and purpose through martial arts and service to their mentor, skilled in weapons ancient and modern. (Correspondence 1, Entropy 1, Life 2, Mind 1, Time 1)</li> <li><b>Social Crusader</b> (Celestial Chorus; Questing) - an eager young person out to change the world with faith and justice, a skilled leader and organizer. (Life 2, Mind 2, Prime 2)</li> <li><b>Bike Messenger</b> (Cult of Ecstasy; Dynamic) - mistress of the streets able to loose herself in the rhythm of the road, in amazing physical shape and able to handle herself in a jam. (Correspondence 1, Entropy 2, Forces 1, Time 2)</li> <li><b>Street Artist</b> (Dreamspeaker; Pattern) - striving to use public art in the form of graffiti, chalk, and other mediums to make viewers aware of issues and to awaken or appease local spirits. (Matter 2, Mind 2, Spirit 2)</li> <li><b>Gambler</b> (Euthanatos; Dynamic) - who lives life by the hand Fate deals them, able to blend in almost anywhere and spot opportunities others would miss. (Entropy 2, Mind 2, Time 2)</li> <li><b>Occult Investigator</b> (Order of Hermes; Pattern) - a private detective specializing in paranormal activities and strange happenings, a skilled investigator and streetwise caseworker trained in the occult and ritual magic. (Correspondence 2, Forces 1, Matter 1, Spirit 2)</li> <li><b>Teenaged Frankenstein</b> (Sons of Ether; Primordial) - a young and overenthusiastic scientific genius prone to recklessness and irresponsibility when experimenting, nerdy but with punk sensibilities. (Forces 2, Life 2, Matter 2)</li> <li><b>Urban Gardener </b>(Verbena; Pattern) - devoted to bringing life and health to the inner city, teaching others about agriculture, nutrition and respect for life. (Life 2, Matter 2, Prime 2)</li> <li><b>Cyberjournalist </b>(Virtual Adept; Questing) - the last of the true investigative reporters, combing the mean streets of the city and the back alleys of the Internet to expose corruption and abuse. (Correspondence 2, Entropy 1, Forces 1, Mind 2)</li> <li><b>Creeper</b> (Hollow One; Dynamic) - an urban explorer breaking into abandoned buildings and closed facilities to uncover the hidden history and secrets of the city. (Connection 1, Entropy 2, Matter 2, Spirit 1)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T09:16:08-07:00","id":1453046,"title":"","content":"Thanks, y'all. This is a good jumping off point.<br /> <br /> I tried to post this on the White Wolf subreddit and they got hung up on needing a full character bio just to give me any advice. Said I was going in reverse. Some of us build our characters to fit a play style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23581-professordetective","name":"ProfessorDetective","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T05:04:44-07:00","id":1453138,"title":"","content":"Just about any kind of mage could be an investigator, but certain styles of investigator lend themselves to certain styles of magic and vice versa.<br /> <br /> The classic noir private detective, for instance, is a perpetual outsider. He has no real place among the police, nor among the criminals but must deal with threats and obligations from both. The classic shaman is a perpetual outsider. He has no real place among the people, nor among the spirits but must deal with threats and obligations from both. You can see where the themes from one naturally align with the themes for the other.<br /> <br /> What kind of detective are you interested in playing? Perhaps there is a magical style that naturally fits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T06:10:10-07:00","id":1453147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453013-help-mage-20th-archetype-characters?p=1453138#post1453138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just about any kind of mage could be an investigator, but certain styles of investigator lend themselves to certain styles of magic and vice versa.<br /> <br /> The classic noir private detective, for instance, is a perpetual outsider. He has no real place among the police, nor among the criminals but must deal with threats and obligations from both. The classic shaman is a perpetual outsider. He has no real place among the people, nor among the spirits but must deal with threats and obligations from both. You can see where the themes from one naturally align with the themes for the other.<br /> <br /> What kind of detective are you interested in playing? Perhaps there is a magical style that naturally fits.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There was there a graphic novel along the lines of &quot;Hard-boiled Shaman!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-22-2021, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:00:34-07:00","id":1453153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ProfessorDetective</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453013-help-mage-20th-archetype-characters?p=1453046#post1453046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, y'all. This is a good jumping off point.<br /> <br /> I tried to post this on the White Wolf subreddit and they got hung up on needing a full character bio just to give me any advice. Said I was going in reverse. Some of us build our characters to fit a play style.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a common sentiment I think, to insist on character story first - so much so that every ST system book I've read says to do it this way. I myself, however, ALWAYS go in reverse. I decide what powers and abilities I want, and then craft a matching story to explain it. I find this method of character creation to be much more satisfying - it's almost as if the character creates itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T20:20:52-07:00","id":1454168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453013-help-mage-20th-archetype-characters?p=1453138#post1453138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just about any kind of mage could be an investigator, but certain styles of investigator lend themselves to certain styles of magic and vice versa.<br /> <br /> The classic noir private detective, for instance, is a perpetual outsider. He has no real place among the police, nor among the criminals but must deal with threats and obligations from both. The classic shaman is a perpetual outsider. He has no real place among the people, nor among the spirits but must deal with threats and obligations from both. You can see where the themes from one naturally align with the themes for the other.<br /> <br /> What kind of detective are you interested in playing? Perhaps there is a magical style that naturally fits.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to Detectives... I always wanted to try writing the REVERSE of a Hard-Boiled Dick: cheerful, mentally stable, does the job more for it's own sake than cash or justice (those never hurt). Like imagine an episode of Jessica Jones, but she's inexplicably been replaced with Kimmy Schmitt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23581-professordetective","name":"ProfessorDetective","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T12:58:55-07:00","id":1456366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ProfessorDetective</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453013-help-mage-20th-archetype-characters?p=1454168#post1454168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it comes to Detectives... I always wanted to try writing the REVERSE of a Hard-Boiled Dick: cheerful, mentally stable, does the job more for it's own sake than cash or justice (those never hurt). Like imagine an episode of Jessica Jones, but she's inexplicably been replaced with Kimmy Schmitt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an amazing idea, and I want to steal it and pitch it to a production company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}